-value and then by descending log(odds ratio). b) Genus coverage histogram. Line represents kernel density estimate fit to the data. c) Boxplots depicting the PGWLS score distribution of significant GO terms with low genus coverage (less than 10%) and of terms with high genus coverage (over 90%). Each dot represents a GO term.
